Gravitational waves of each harmonic mode are calculated by integrating $\Psi_4^{l,m,\infty}$ twice in time:
\begin{align}
  h^{l,m,\infty}(t_\text{ret}) &= h^{l,m,\infty}_+ (t_\text{ret}) - i h^{l,m,\infty}_\times(t_\text{ret}) \nonumber\\
  &= - \int^{t_\text{ret}} dt'\int^{t'} \Psi_4^{l,m,\infty}(t'')dt''.
\end{align}
For the time integration, we employ the fixed frequency method~\cite{Reisswig:2010di} by
\begin{align}
  h^{l,m,\infty}(t_\text{ret}) = \int df' \frac{\tilde{\Psi}_4^{l,m,\infty}(f')}{(2\pi\max[f',f_\text{cut}])^2} \exp(2\pi i f' t_\text{ret}),
\end{align}
where $\tilde{\Psi}_4^{l,m,\infty}(f)$ is the Fourier component of $\Psi_4^{l,m,\infty}(t)$ and $f_\text{cut}$ is set to be $0.8m\Omega_0/(2\pi)$.

