Figures~\ref{fig:model_comp_27} and \ref{fig:model_comp_25}  show the difference of the tidal-part phase and amplitude between our inspiral waveform model~\eqref{eq:phimodel} and \eqref{eq:Amodel} and the hybrid waveforms for the models with ${\cal M}_c= 1.1752\,M_\odot$ and  ${\cal M}_c= 1.0882\,M_\odot$. Here, the phase difference between the tidal-part phase of hybrid waveforms, $\Psi_{\rm Hybrid}^{\rm tidal}$, and that of our inspiral waveform model, $\Psi_{\rm model}^{\rm tidal}$, is computed by
\begin{align}
